Ritsu client patch 2 of 2: local profiles (apply after client-offline.patch).

osu!local profiles (osu.Game/LocalPriority) decide who is playing:
- OfflineAPIProvider implements ILocalProfileApi, so the active profile is the player and new scores are saved under it.
- Profile page, switcher and settings tab: the toolbar account button shows the active profile (click: profile page,
  right-click: switcher). Ctrl+P and /profile, /top, /import replay open the profile page or import into the active profile.
  The switcher's top row is "Guest" (Ritsu has no online account); the online lookup settings are left out.
- Play recording (finished, failed, quit or restarted attempts), mod rules and auto-switch rules, profile pictures and flags,
  local beatmap tags, "count everything as ranked" and Relax / Autopilot PP options.
- Score context menu: "Transfer score" and "Exclude from PP" (play, difficulty or beatmap set); difficulty and beatmap set
  menus exclude them from PP too. Replay import and export (top or all replays) from the profile menu.
- Profile page: judgement counts shortened from 10,000 on (417.4k, exact count in the tooltip); lists expanded with
  "show more" stay expanded until a beatmap is entered (played or watched as a replay); hiding the cover is always saved.

Ritsu's own profile data (RitsuProfileManager) is kept underneath: RitsuProfileBridge keeps the Ritsu profile with the same
name active (created when missing), because these still read it:
- commands, library memos and marked scores, collections, song select play-history filters;
- per-profile playtime (RitsuPlaytime) and the "Local profile playtime method" setting;
- the leaderboard scope for the active profile vs all profiles (RitsuLeaderboardScope). While an osu!local profile is
  active, its "Local" scope, personal best and the local rank on beatmaps use that profile's own scores, so transfers show;
- the local ranked status (status pill, classic info panel, mod select), which also follows the PP exclusions above;
- "Export original replay" and exporting replays under the profile name.

The command palette's /whatif and /reach project from the osu!local profile's PP while one is active.

Builds together with client-offline.patch. Tests for Ritsu's profile logic are included.

